  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABHYeLxw",
      "title": "proxyd: add opt-in rate limiting by authenticated alias",
      "author": "bitwiseguy",
      "number": 761,
      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAddresses task 3 of this [RPC Hardening notion doc](https://app.notion.com/p/oplabs/RPC-Hardening-Work-Planning-3e6f153ee16280ea8fb8c3bc66ea4789).\r\n\r\nAdd opt-in `[rate_limit] use_auth_alias` so authenticated consumers sharing an egress IP get independent rate-limit buckets.\r\n\r\nBase and method limits use the configured alias across HTTP requests, batch elements, and mapped WebSocket calls, with isolated buckets in memory and Redis. Unauthenticated requests retain IP-based limits. Default behavior and existing exemptions remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\nNew tests added that cover...\r\n\r\n- Independent quotas for different aliases sharing an IP.\r\n- Shared quotas across IPs and credentials using the same alias.\r\n- Disabled-mode compatibility and alias/IP bucket isolation.\r\n- Redis quota sharing across replicas.\r\n- Batch rejection handling and HTTP/WS quota sharing.\r\n- Rejection metrics attributed by alias.\r\n\r\nThe full proxyd test suite and focused race checks passed.\r\n\r\n## Related Issues\r\n\r\n* Closes https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/core-team/issues/3251\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-08T17:18:54Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-09T20:37:39Z",
      "additions": 462,
      "deletions": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABN67PNQ",
      "title": "enable tx validation trace logging",
      "author": "yashvardhan-kukreja",
      "number": 797,
      "body": "Signed-off-by: Yashvardhan Kukreja <yashvardhan@oplabs.co>\r\n\r\n<!-- Contributions welcome! See https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md -->\r\n\r\n**Description**\r\n\r\nAdds two Info logs to each tx validation request, emitted from `httptrace` hooks: `tx validation conn queued` when the request starts waiting for a pooled connection, and `tx validation got conn` with `conn_queued_ms` when it gets one. \r\n\r\nBoth carry `req_id`. This helps troubleshoot tx validation timeouts during traffic bursts by showing whether the time went to the connection pool (a `conn queued` with no `got conn`) or to the tx validation middleware (`got conn`, then a timeout).\r\n\r\nI chose logs over metrics because per-request timing is detailed enough for troubleshooting but too detailed to alert on or chart trends from, and Info level because two short lines per request adds little log volume.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\nPlease describe any tests you've added. If you've added no tests, or left important behavior untested, please explain why not.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nAdd any other context about the problem you're solving.\r\n\r\n**Metadata**\r\n\r\n- Fixes #[Link to Issue]\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-09T18:39:42Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-09T19:01:51Z",
      "additions": 95,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABNbv-_Q",
      "title": "fix(proxyd): rate limit method override semantics",
      "author": "yashvardhan-kukreja",
      "number": 796,
      "body": "Signed-off-by: Yashvardhan Kukreja <yashvardhan@oplabs.co>\r\n\r\n<!-- Contributions welcome! See https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md -->\r\n\r\n**Description**\r\n\r\nThe rate-limit-method-overrides never overrode the base rate-limits. Instead they applied on top of the base-rate-limits. That doesn't make much sense with the concept of \"overrides\" and makes it impossible to loosen the rate limit of a specific method compared to the base rate.\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes that by either applying the base-rate-limit on the incoming request OR the method-override if it exists for the incoming request's RPC method.\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\nPlease describe any tests you've added. If you've added no tests, or left important behavior untested, please explain why not.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nAdd any other context about the problem you're solving.\r\n\r\n**Metadata**\r\n\r\n- Fixes #[Link to Issue]\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-06T23:56:30Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-09T19:30:29Z",
      "additions": 20,
      "deletions": 16
    }
